WEBVTT

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:16.120
<i>The anisotropic being Yaha-kui zaShunina, 
who appeared at Haneda airport,</i>

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.930
<i>offered the Japanese government
devices capable of</i>

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.710
<i>creating infinite electricity, called the Wam.</i>

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:28.250
<i>Yaha-kui zaShunina wanted the Wam 
to be used by all of humanity.</i>

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:33.470
<i>However, the United Nations 
Security Council demanded that</i>

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:36.090
<i>the Japanese government surrender 
the Wam unconditionally.</i>

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:41.990
<i>The Prime Minister of Japan, 
Inuzuka Kozo, was at a crossroads,</i>

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:46.650
<i>when Shindo Kojiro made a proposal.</i>

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:48.980
Me?

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.160
Nanoka

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:45.850
Target: the Kado object in front of us.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.400
AP rounds loaded!

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:48.850
Fire!

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:03.450
Local Response Team Forward Base
for Large Cube That Appeared on 7/25

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:06.650
<i>On the 30th of this month, the UN Security 
Council voted to demand that all "Wam,"</i>

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:10.710
<i>the new energy source given by the 
anisotropic to the Japanese government,</i>

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:11.710
<i>be handed over to the UN.</i>

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:17.210
UN Security Council 
votes to demand all Wam be handed over

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:20.020
<i>In an emergency meeting held the same day, 
a vote was held to make a declaration</i>

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:23.720
<i>including punitive measures toward 
Japan if its demands were not met,</i>

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:29.220
<i>which was voted for by all members 
of the security council except Japan.</i>

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:27.030
One, two, three, four...

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:30.280
Two, two, three, four...

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:35.170
<i>These punitive measures are to 
include "all necessary steps,"</i>

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:33.750
Three, two, three, four...

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:36.490
Four, two, three, four...

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:40.460
<i>which includes economic sanctions, 
as well as international military action.</i>

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:40.000
Five, two, three, four...

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:42.530
So it includes sanctions, huh?

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.360
That's fast.

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:45.830
This is unusual.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.290
Just shows how dangerous 
these things are.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:53.730
They probably decided they're more dangerous 
than chemical or nuclear weapons.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:57.710
Public opinion's going to lean 
toward handing them over, I bet.

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:00.880
Nobody wants to fight the whole world.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:03.640
The normal way to look at it is that

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:06.530
the government has no choice 
but to hand over the Wam.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:09.140
The problem is...

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.790
What's the anisotropic 
going to think about that?

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.020
On your mark...

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:14.360
Go!

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:22.460
Military action...

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:24.780
It was just part of the resolution.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.810
It's not like the UN military will 
launch an attack right away.

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:32.040
Are we going to have a 
war with the UN military?

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:35.410
If the lives of our citizens are in danger,

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:38.650
we have to fight to defend ourselves.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:42.050
We're the self-defense forces, after all.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:50.760
So humans are fighting over a source 
of energy that will save all humanity?

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:55.470
Is this what you want, Anisotropic Being?

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:59.490
Sergeant Agata, you've got a call from HQ.

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:02.060
They want the unit to provide an escort.

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:03.650
Not the cops?

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:05.830
They're heading to...

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:18.270
<b>JGSDF Mishuku Garrison</b>

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:17.050
Mishuku, huh?

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:22.760
What does an anisotropic 
being want with a garrison?

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:22.760
<b>Defense Ministry Technology Research HQ
Electronic Equipment Lab Experiment Wing</b>

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:26.140
There's a Defense Ministry lab here.

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:31.180
A tech lab... So it has to do with the Wam?

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:34.070
The anisotropic being, the Wam, the lab...

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:39.070
It's hard to say whether this is good or bad.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:45.820
Um... I'd like to go back.

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:50.100
Um, our Wam experiments are 
just starting to get really good,

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:50.340
<b>EMI/RFI Shielded Room</b>

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.340
and our research is going super fast!

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:54.960
I can't afford to lose a single second!

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:58.100
I just want to go back right now!

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:00.130
Hello? Um—

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:03.050
Then you should be here.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.550
The anisotropic being!

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:21.850
Dr. Shinawa, the anisotropic 
being is not edible.

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:24.860
We don't know that for sure! If I try hard...

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:28.480
She is appropriate.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:35.410
Dr. Shinawa is a student of 
yours, right, Dr. Mifune?

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:40.400
She's just part of my lab.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:43.210
I'd never go so far as to 
call myself her teacher.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:47.920
She's a far greater scientist 
than I'll ever be, anyway.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:51.590
You won the Nobel Prize, right?

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:55.140
She's going to win ten of them.

00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:57.680
What's she like?

00:06:58.090 --> 00:07:00.040
Definitely a genius,

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:02.180
but she has her problems.

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:06.980
She's like a ball of pure potential...

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:08.610
I know.

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:10.760
She's a child.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:16.820
97% of all the Wam produced are right here.

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:24.630
My first time touching one with my bare hands!

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:29.660
Whoops...

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:33.350
I see! I see!

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:34.140
Huh?

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:36.620
Um... This one is...

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:38.620
Shindo, I'll put you in charge here.

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:38.890
Why? Why? Why?

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:40.810
I'm going to the next place.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:44.440
Tsukai-san will stay with you while I'm here.

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:46.650
Don't do anything too crazy.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:48.240
Crazy?

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:50.530
If you don't know, that's fine.

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:10.860
The waves are starting to 
spread throughout the country.

00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:15.580
As time passes, the confusion will grow.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:19.550
If the government makes the wrong call,

00:08:19.550 --> 00:08:22.480
Japan will end up fighting the whole world...

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:26.610
Thanks to the Wam you brought.

00:08:27.850 --> 00:08:30.170
I shouldn't have given them the Wam?

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:33.840
I'm saying there must have been another way.

00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:36.570
There was another way,

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:38.340
and there still is.

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:40.920
Methods.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.230
Possibilities.

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:44.280
All of them are endless.

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:48.090
I chose one of them, and acted.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:52.260
The Wam should be given to humanity,

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:55.310
and must spread to them 
all as soon as possible.

00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:58.640
Because that is...

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:02.060
the right answer.

00:09:04.490 --> 00:09:08.740
I think humanity should never 
have been given the Wam.

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:12.100
Our opinions differ.

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:15.070
<b>Hand over the Wam now!</b>

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:15.070
<b>Inuzuka should
resign!</b>

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:15.940
Hand over the Wam now!

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:17.780
Do you want a war?

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:20.580
The cabinet must resign immediately!

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:23.700
Inuzuka! Resign!

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:36.510
I suppose I should say it's nice to meet you.

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:41.640
I am the Japanese Prime 
Minister, Inuzuka Kozo.

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:44.130
I'm Yaha-kui zaShunina.

00:09:57.570 --> 00:09:58.690
Chief Cabinet Secretary,

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:03.450
the Security Council has demanded that 
all nations put sanctions into place.

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:06.170
If Japan does not turn over the Wam,

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:10.030
they're prepared to freeze the accounts 
of all Japanese individuals and companies.

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:13.020
And in addition...

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:13.630
What?

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:16.630
The JSDF patrols have confirmed that...

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:22.430
a carrier strike force is leaving Yokosuka.

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:24.850
Calm down.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:28.370
Nobody's stupid enough to start launching 
missiles at us out of nowhere.

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:29.740
They're just applying pressure.

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:32.890
But that doesn't change the fact 
that we need to respond fast.

00:10:32.890 --> 00:10:35.930
They'll put those economic sanctions 
into place without hesitation.

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:37.650
I know that.

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:42.070
That's why we're accepting 
this strange situation.

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:49.830
You're the one who wanted to publicize 
the meeting at the airport to the media.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:54.920
I thought you didn't like 
meeting in secret like this.

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:57.470
I am only acting out of necessity.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:10:59.090
Necessity?

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:03.830
Shindo and Dr. Shinawa Kanata 
are currently in a shielded room

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:07.660
owned by the JSDF, working hard.

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:11.360
I chose a shielded room because 
of the incredible amount

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:14.940
of concentration required for the process.

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:20.120
I wanted to remove anything that 
would interfere with mental processes.

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:22.660
Electromagnetic waves 
could hurt concentration?

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:23.460
Correct.

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:29.200
Human bodies aren't made to receive EM waves.

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:31.430
That is your understanding.

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:35.880
We lack the ability to prove you wrong.

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:38.330
They are hurrying,

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:42.720
because the time limit set for your answer 
by the UN Security Council is approaching.

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:47.230
In other words, what's needed now is speed.

00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:50.500
Yes, I've heard from Shindo.

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:55.040
He said you possess a way out of this situation.

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:57.470
It's not difficult.

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.900
Once Shindo's preparations are complete,

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:02.020
it can be carried out immediately.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:07.990
However, you are the one who 
will make that decision.

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:12.890
In order to bring you closer 
to the right answer,

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:18.130
I want to talk with you, 
Prime Minister Inuzuka.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:39.480
She's investigating the way they're placed?

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.990
She's thinking hard.

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:44.530
That's what her face looks 
like when her mind is racing.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:50.340
If she's using her full mental strength...

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:52.870
What about him?

00:12:55.250 --> 00:13:01.390
The Wam are a source of power more 
than sufficient for humanity's needs.

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:05.260
But there is still a struggle
 going on for them.

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:09.540
At the core of the problem 
is the concept of difference.

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:10.570
Difference?

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:11.890
"Difference."

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:13.020
I see.

00:13:13.550 --> 00:13:17.200
Human society is divided 
into nations by borders,

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:20.020
with each nation having its own interests.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:23.530
The spinodal decomposition process 
where the difference

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:29.150
in temperature and density between nations 
retrogresses from equilibrium is in stagnation.

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:30.950
Spinodal...

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:39.490
Country A stops bread 
from going to Country B.

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:44.610
Country B wants to steal 
bread from Country A.

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:49.060
The same thing takes place between 
geographical areas, between ethnic groups,

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:51.040
and at every layer.

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:53.600
That's a economic problem.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:56.260
But this is, in fact, a misunderstanding.

00:13:56.880 --> 00:13:59.010
The Wam are not a limited amount of bread.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:01.700
They do not need to be divided among you.

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:08.200
They are an infinite spring that will 
rain down upon all of humanity.

00:14:10.210 --> 00:14:12.910
We took the Wam.

00:14:13.380 --> 00:14:15.500
In all the chaos, we may still not have noted

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.880
the full implications of this.

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:21.170
But I believe we can imagine

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:28.170
a way for all of humanity to surpass 
national interests and prosper as a whole.

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:31.900
Who should think of that way?

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:33.500
You?

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:36.770
<i>Or the leader of another country?</i>

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.340
<i>The United Nations?</i>

00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:40.440
<i>Or...</i>

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:41.670
me?

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:49.000
Human prosperity should be 
decided upon by humanity,

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:52.700
and all of us should do the thinking.

00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:08.240
A moment ago, a certain person told me 
that the Wam had put humanity into chaos.

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:09.960
That conflict was occurring.

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:13.440
<i>That the Wam should never have been given.</i>

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:15.470
<i>That is not correct.</i>

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:20.200
It's true that the conflict 
over the Wam is a sad thing.

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:24.480
It's possible that someone may die over it.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:28.130
But that is not the fault of the Wam.

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:30.070
That is humanity's responsibility.

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:33.580
The Wam are neither good nor evil.

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:35.340
They're just a source of power.

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:39.520
The responsibility for them lies 
with the one who uses them.

00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:43.240
Even if the result is disaster,

00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:45.340
that is not the fault of the Wam,

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:48.270
let alone you, the anisotropic.

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:52.590
Thinking that you've done 
something wrong to humanity is,

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:57.960
in fact, rude and arrogant.

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:01.890
Prime Minister Inuzuka.

00:16:07.550 --> 00:16:09.900
I offer you a suggestion.

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:26.790
I see...

00:16:27.850 --> 00:16:32.100
I didn't understand anything...

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:41.770
Prime Minister.

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:45.350
Prime Minister Inuzuka.

00:16:49.060 --> 00:16:52.110
Send a message to all domestic 
and foreign media organizations.

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:53.570
Then...

00:16:53.940 --> 00:16:55.690
We're giving them Japan's response.

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:58.070
Call an emergency press conference.

00:16:58.580 --> 00:16:59.460
Yes, sir!

00:17:07.810 --> 00:17:12.510
Any press conference right now has 
to be about their answer to the UN.

00:17:13.160 --> 00:17:15.010
Yeah, it has to be.

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:25.140
There they are.

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:31.650
Shindo Kojiro, the representative 
of the anisotropic, and...

00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:34.020
Who's that?

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:37.510
It is now 6:00 PM.

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:39.170
Now...

00:17:39.170 --> 00:17:43.270
<i>Prime Minister Inuzuka will hereby 
hold an emergency press conference.</i>

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:48.390
<i>Given the importance of this conference,</i>

00:17:48.390 --> 00:17:52.460
<i>there will be no restrictions 
on audio or video recording,</i>

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:54.170
<i>as well as internet uploads.</i>

00:17:56.430 --> 00:17:58.720
Did he just say something weird?

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:08.910
I would like to share a message from Japan 
to the United Nations Security Council,

00:18:08.910 --> 00:18:10.930
as well as all the peoples of the world.

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:16.450
Five days ago, our nation was given the Wam,

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:21.740
a new energy source, by Yaha-kui zaShunina, 
a visitor from the anisotropic.

00:18:22.550 --> 00:18:27.060
We tried to find a way to share the Wam's 
benefits with all the world's people,

00:18:27.060 --> 00:18:30.500
regardless of nationality.

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:37.510
<b>Prime Minister Inuzuka Emergency Press Conference</b>

00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:34.360
<i>But yesterday we received a resolution</i>

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:37.510
<i>from the UN Security Council 
that included sanctions.</i>

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:43.010
<i>As the Prime Minister of Japan, 
this situation gravely concerns me.</i>

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:49.780
I am here to tell you that we will accept 
all the Security Council's demands

00:18:49.780 --> 00:18:56.550
and hand over all 196 Wam 
that Japan possesses.

00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:59.470
Well, it's not like they had a choice.

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:03.140
We will work with the United 
Nations to turn them over

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:03.770
So the Wam are on their way to the UN, huh?

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:07.250
immediately, as soon as 
both parties are ready.

00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:07.250
So the Wam are passing 
right out of Japan's hands

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:10.460
and right into those of the major powers...

00:19:08.770 --> 00:19:10.460
And now...

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:13.150
In addition to handing over the Wam,

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:20.060
I would also like to publicize the results of 
our national lab's research into the Wam.

00:19:21.380 --> 00:19:23.470
Research?

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:31.240
I am here as the representative of the 
anisotropic being Yaha-kui zaShunina.

00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:32.980
My name is Shindo Kojiro.

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:39.250
Dr. Shinawa of the Unified Science Research 
Lab's Wam Research and Analysis Unit

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:42.070
<i>will now announce her findings.</i>

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:43.930
Okay!

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:50.330
I would appreciate it if all media would 
move their cameras to record her hands.

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:53.040
Okay, I'll make this simple...

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:59.700
So, as you all know, the Wam are a 
source of energy from the anisotropic.

00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:03.340
As for how they generate that energy...

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:05.610
It's their form.

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:07.250
Their shape.

00:20:07.870 --> 00:20:10.630
The Wam have an anisotropic form,

00:20:10.630 --> 00:20:13.550
which is why they can 
access anisotropic energy.

00:20:13.550 --> 00:20:18.790
It's like they're an anisotropically 
shaped hole that energy flows out from.

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:25.370
In other words, what's important is the shape, 
not so much what they're made of.

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:31.260
There's a trick to it,

00:20:31.260 --> 00:20:33.010
but once you know the trick...

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:51.560
<i>There you go.</i>

00:20:52.530 --> 00:20:55.060
That's how you make a Wam!

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:03.860
Wh-What did she say? <i>Make</i> a Wam?

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:07.200
How to make a Wam?!

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:07.870
Hey!

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:12.270
The Japanese government has just 
made an important announcement!

00:21:12.270 --> 00:21:16.780
The Japanese government has publicized their 
investigations into how to make a Wam!

00:21:16.780 --> 00:21:21.380
The media has just now shared this 
information with the whole world!

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:25.050
The Wam are going to spread 
throughout the world!

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:29.310
196 Wam are meaningless now!

00:21:29.310 --> 00:21:32.050
Everybody who wants one can make his own!

00:21:32.050 --> 00:21:34.160
Japan is out of control!

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.600
Society will collapse!

00:21:35.730 --> 00:21:38.650
Can the Japanese government 
take responsibility for this?!

00:21:37.670 --> 00:21:40.230
How do you intend to handle 
terrorism with these?!

00:21:40.230 --> 00:21:42.360
<i>There's no way to predict the effect of this.</i>

00:21:42.750 --> 00:21:44.950
<i>Conflict, accidents...</i>

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:47.460
<i>Blood will be shed because of this.</i>

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:52.640
<i>The Prime Minister knew this and 
chose to spread the Wam anyway.</i>

00:21:53.430 --> 00:21:57.260
<i>We're headed toward a new world, 
even if it means bloodshed.</i>

00:21:57.900 --> 00:21:59.410
<i>This is...</i>

00:21:59.930 --> 00:22:01.110
<i>a revolution!</i>

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:37.000
Friend.

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:38.360
A vague concept.

00:23:38.360 --> 00:23:40.230
Few can make the Wam now,

00:23:40.230 --> 00:23:41.450
but more are learning.

00:23:41.450 --> 00:23:43.020
A real revolution is coming.

00:23:43.020 --> 00:23:45.690
If you needed a two-kilometer 
empty region near Kanto...

00:23:45.690 --> 00:23:48.070
Districts 1 through 3 have been evacuated.

00:23:48.070 --> 00:23:49.900
Shindo, the next one.

00:23:48.500 --> 00:23:52.000
Tetrok
